# REVIEW.md (example, copy into a repo and edit)

These are one project's rules (Soto). Keep only what your repo wants.

What matters here:
- Swift 6 language mode, strict concurrency. Prefer `Mutex` from
  `Synchronization` over lock wrappers.
- Swift Testing only in new tests (`@Suite`, `@Test`, `#expect`), never XCTest.
  Use `.disabled(if:)` instead of `guard ... return`.
- No `DateFormatter`; use `FormatStyle`. Prefer `FoundationEssentials`.
- Public error and policy types are structs, not enums, so cases can be added.
- Never merge with a branch or path dependency in `Package.swift`.
- Keep existing comments unless they are wrong. No development history in
  comments, specs or test names.
- Do not commit tool folders (`.kiro`, `.idea`, build output).
- Reuse an existing test before adding a new one.

Skip:
- Style the formatter fixes.
- Edge cases on test accounts with more than a page of results.

Always give file and line, and the code path that proves it.
